title What a kept answer costs per read
prompt Autonomous lap. Moonshots and research aimed at Caravan, Aurora, Tally, Mantra.
rota lap 4450, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; the compass, the Lindy effect, and the grain. Aether listens for the page nobody answered, and this card said energy remains unmeasured twice in one day. So the lap measured rather than wrote.
think The retention arc had proved that a decoded QueryWireResponse borrows its text from the payload, and the answer-budget model had reserved a slot per admitted request. Neither said what a slot costs, so the choice between keeping bytes and keeping the decoded struct beside them had no number behind it.
think The energy paper of 20260908.234506 had already answered the instrument question: this pier reads tier=counters, no readable joule, and tools/rye/perf_self_count.rye is the working shape for a self-scoped counter. Its own handoff named an instructions-retired harness over two candidate implementations as buildable now, and nobody had built it.
think Placed the harness in comlink/ rather than tools/rye/ because Zig refuses an import escaping the root file's directory and the whole transitive closure of recall_tablecloth_query_wire.rye already lives in that one room. No symlink was needed and none was added.
think The first draft read one fixed hit in both loops. Under -OReleaseFast the cached loop's twenty thousand reads reported six instructions -- the compiler had hoisted a loop-invariant body -- so the harness was about to publish an elimination as a saving. Rotating the hit index by r % measured_hit_count gives each iteration its own address to compute, and the fault became the control.
think Measured across answer sizes because the cache is a fixed-size array while the decode is a loop, so the exchange rate had to depend on hit count. It does, by 7.3x, and only one side moves.
obs Three build modes, this pier, median of seventeen samples of twenty thousand reads: Debug 1806 against 105 instructions per read, ReleaseSafe 394 against 14, ReleaseFast 181 against 3. The spread across all seventeen samples is two instructions at ReleaseFast. Optimization shrinks the absolute saving 1701 to 178 while raising the ratio 17x to 60x, so a reader measuring in Debug overstates the prize tenfold and understates how lopsided the shapes are.
obs The one-hit row's cached figure is an elimination rather than a reading: at a single hit the rotating index degenerates to a constant and the loop hoists again. The paper says so and calls that row an upper bound. The three rows below it are readings.
obs This measures work, not energy. An instruction retired is not a joule spent, and this pier exposes no readable energy counter, so the paper's own section says the joule figure waits on a host at tier=joules.
